course: dictionary
lesson: 11479
title: Affiliation: belonging and connection
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Affiliation is a noun, and it is about belonging. Its first meaning is an official connection with a group, club, party or organisation. «The team has an affiliation with the local football club» means the team is officially linked to that club.
explain: Its second meaning is about feelings: the sense of belonging to a group. «Sam felt a strong affiliation with his school» tells you Sam felt that he belonged there. The word «strong» is a clue that this is about feelings.
explain: Look for clue words in the context. Forms often ask about affiliation, as in «party affiliation» or «religious affiliation». These phrases ask which party or religion you belong to. «In affiliation with» means officially linked to.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Affiliation» means an official connection with a group, club, party or organisation.
fact: «Affiliation» can also mean the feeling of belonging to a group.
fact: Useful phrases: «party affiliation», «religious affiliation» and «in affiliation with».
fact: «Affiliation» is a noun, and its plural is «affiliations».
exercise: «The club is in affiliation with the national sports body.» What does «in affiliation with» mean? | Far away from | Against the rules of | Paid for by | *Officially connected to
exercise: A form asks for your «party affiliation». What is it asking for? | Your home address | How tall you are | *Which party you belong to or support | Your favourite colour
exercise: «Sam felt a strong affiliation with his school.» Which word in this sentence names the feeling of belonging? | strong | school | *affiliation | felt
test: «Her religious affiliation is written on the form.» What does religious affiliation mean? | Her favourite prayer | The church she painted last summer | A religious song she likes to sing | *The religion she belongs to
test: «The shop has an affiliation with a large chain.» What does affiliation mean here? | A big discount on every item | A feeling of sadness | A type of shop sign | *An official connection
exam: Which best describes affiliation? | A type of food | To run very fast | The name of a plant | *An official connection to a group, or the feeling of belonging to one
